@startuml Selector Priority Algorithm
!theme plain

title TestCaptive - Smart Selector Priority Algorithm

start

:Element Detected;

if (Has data-testid?) then (yes)
  :Use Test ID Selector;
  note right
    **Priority: 1 (Highest)**
    Stability: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
    Example: [data-testid="submit-btn"]
    
    **Why Best:**
    - Explicitly for testing
    - Never changes
    - Unique by design
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (Has aria-label?) then (yes)
  :Use ARIA Label Selector;
  note right
    **Priority: 2**
    Stability: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
    Example: [aria-label="Submit Form"]
    
    **Why Good:**
    - Accessibility standard
    - Semantic meaning
    - Rarely changes
    
    **Frameworks:** Playwright
    (Uses aria-label for accessible selectors)
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (Has id attribute?) then (yes)
  :Use ID Selector;
  note right
    **Priority: 3**
    Stability: ⭐⭐⭐
    Example: #submit-button
    
    **Why OK:**
    - Should be unique
    - Fast lookup
    
    **Risk:**
    - May be auto-generated
    - Can change in refactoring
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (Has name attribute?) then (yes)
  :Use Name Selector;
  note right
    **Priority: 4**
    Stability: ⭐⭐
    Example: [name="username"]
    
    **Why Acceptable:**
    - Common for forms
    
    **Risk:**
    - Not always unique
    - Backend-driven
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (Has xpath?) then (yes)
  :Use XPath Selector;
  note right
    **Priority: 5**
    Stability: ⭐
    Example: //form[@id="login"]//button
    
    **Why Risky:**
    - Breaks with DOM changes
    - Fragile
    
    **Only When:**
    No better option available
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Use CSS Selector (Fallback);
note right
  **Priority: 6 (Last Resort)**
  Stability: ⚠️
  Example: .btn.btn-primary.submit
  
  **Why Worst:**
  - CSS classes for styling
  - Changes frequently
  - Rarely unique
  
  **Enterprise Enhancement:**
  Should generate relative selector
  using parent context
end note

stop

floating note left
  **Algorithm Benefits:**
  
  ✅ Deterministic
  ✅ Prioritizes stability
  ✅ Framework-aware
  ✅ Graceful fallback
  
  **Enterprise TODO:**
  
  🔄 Validate uniqueness
  🔄 Score selectors
  🔄 Use parent context
  🔄 AI optimization
end note

@enduml
